// yes-no.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for typed answers (docs/01 Part I section 10b): YES and NO are
// ordinary in-world actions. A game that asks the player something reads
// the reply with `on yes` / `on no`, and a `when` guard scopes each
// question to its moment, so several questions can live in one game
// without ever answering for each other. Untended, YES and NO get a dry
// flavor line; they are never meta, answering is speech, and it happens
// in the story. Compile and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/yes-no.storyarc -o yes-no.z5
//   frotz yes-no.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   yes                  talking to nobody about nothing: the flavor line
//   talk to innkeeper    the standard TALK verb; he asks his question
//   no                   the guarded `on no` answers, the offer closes
//   talk to innkeeper    ask again
//   yes                  the guarded `on yes` this time: a room is yours
//   talk to innkeeper    he has nothing further to ask
//   yes                  back to the flavor line: no question is open

game
    title  "The Last Room"
    headline "A yes-no showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  taproom

summon.statusline

flag asking_room
flag room_taken

room taproom
    name "The Taproom"
    desc "Low beams, a cold hearth, and an innkeeper polishing the counter."

thing innkeeper of character in taproom
    name "innkeeper"
    words innkeeper, keeper
    desc "A patient man with exactly one room to his name."

    on talk
        if room_taken
            say "\"Settled in already, no? Mind the third step.\""
            stop
        change asking_room to true
        say "\"One room left tonight. Will you take it?\""

on yes when asking_room
    change asking_room to false
    change room_taken to true
    say "\"Good.\" He slides a key across the counter. \"Top of the
         stairs, mind the third step.\""

on no when asking_room
    change asking_room to false
    say "\"Suit yourself.\" He goes back to his polishing."
